From: Ze kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 13c] ppp: retain exact owner through IPv6 control transmit

PRIVATE SOURCE ONLY after Ze v7.3 + 0001..0005 + reviewed 0007..0011
successors + frozen 0012/0012a/0013a/0013aa and 0013b. No ioctl dispatch,
feature bit, or Go activation. Main owns exact composed application, kernel
compile and native proof; this source packet is not a runtime verdict.

Socket binding remains immutable. TX authority is stamped before LOCAL_OUT,
survives skb->sk orphaning and extension loss as a copied required bit, and
is consumed only by the original PPP writer before lower transport. Ordinary
RX receipts never become TX restrictions. Native IPv6 fragmentation, checksum,
multicast loopback and generic prelookup protocol feedback remain native.
Owned route writers, multicast operations and option escape producers use the
retained original object; numeric labels never authorize a replacement.

--- a/include/net/ppp_control.h
+++ b/include/net/ppp_control.h
@@ -88,2 +88,18 @@
 void ppp_control_scrub(struct sk_buff *skb);
+
+/* sk MUST have native syscall, queue, or socket-RCU lifetime throughout the
+ * borrow. Binding is immutable until inet6 cleanup; no numeric lookup.
+ */
+struct ppp_control_owner *ppp_control_sock_owner(const struct sock *sk);
+/* These predicates protect their original-device reads internally. */
+bool ppp_control_sock_dev(const struct sock *sk, const struct net_device *dev);
+struct dst_entry;
+bool ppp_control_sock_dst(const struct sock *sk, const struct dst_entry *dst);
+bool ppp_control_sock_index(const struct sock *sk, int ifindex);
+/* LOCAL_OUT stamps before callbacks can orphan sk. The copied skb bit MUST
+ * keep TX required after extension loss. Only original PPP handoff or a new
+ * physical PPP receive boundary may consume it.
+ */
+int ppp_control_tx_prepare(struct sock *sk, struct sk_buff *skb);
+bool ppp_control_tx_dev(const struct sk_buff *skb, const struct net_device *dev);
 
